Species Biological Information Database — implementation complete.

How to run
  bash setup.sh                 # checks python3/sqlite3, prepares DATA_DIR (no packages needed)
  PORT=8000 bash run.sh         # serves http://127.0.0.1:8000 in the foreground
  DATA_DIR (optional, default ./data) holds species.db; sample species are loaded when empty.

Files
  server.py   Python standard-library HTTP server + SQLite, server-rendered HTML (no JS framework)
  setup.sh    dependency/runtime check and data-directory preparation
  run.sh      starts server.py with PORT and DATA_DIR (default 8000 / ./data)

Features (all reachable from the menu in the header)
  Home           counts (records, threatened species, kingdoms), browse-by-kingdom links, featured species
  Browse & Search list of species; search text matches common/scientific name, family, class, description;
                 filters for kingdom, conservation status, habitat, diet; sort by name, scientific name,
                 length, lifespan; shows "Showing X of Y species"
  Species detail full record, with Edit record and Delete record (with confirmation)
  Add Species    form with validation (required fields, allowed options, numeric values >= 0, unique scientific name)
  Edit           same form pre-filled, validated the same way
  About          describes the data and how to use the site

Design choices (made without asking)
  - Base background: linen (#FAF0E6). Maroon (#800000) for the header/nav, buttons, table headers,
    badges, card borders, headings, links, flash and error boxes, footer.
  - Storage: SQLite file in DATA_DIR; 13 sample species seeded when the table is empty.
  - Pages are plain server-rendered HTML forms, so they work in Chromium without JavaScript
    (the only script is a delete confirmation).

